1
00:00:01,679 --> 00:00:03,681
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,352 --> 00:01:33,687
- [crackling]
- [panting]

3
00:01:34,897 --> 00:01:39,902
[Gosha grunting]

4
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:43,489
Wow. You're a much more
forceful kid than I thought.

5
00:01:43,572 --> 00:01:44,615
[gasps]

6
00:01:45,116 --> 00:01:47,368
No wonder Legoshi fell for you.

7
00:01:47,451 --> 00:01:49,036
[Haru] How do you know--

8
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,788
Look here.

9
00:01:50,871 --> 00:01:53,040
He and I have similar eyes.
Don't you think?

10
00:01:53,707 --> 00:01:54,875
{\an8}Surely you're not--

11
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:57,920
{\an8}Yeah, I'm his grandpa. [chuckles]

12
00:01:58,003 --> 00:01:59,004
{\an8}[gasping]

13
00:01:59,213 --> 00:02:01,006
{\an8}But... you're a lizard.

14
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:04,260
- [stun gun crackling]
- [screaming]

15
00:02:04,343 --> 00:02:09,265
THE DEMON KING OF BEASTS

16
00:02:09,348 --> 00:02:11,350
[gentle music playing]

17
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:15,104
I'm sorry again about the stun gun thing.

18
00:02:15,187 --> 00:02:17,731
I didn't know Legoshi
was related to a lizard.

19
00:02:18,065 --> 00:02:19,400
[Gosha] I'm not offended.

20
00:02:19,984 --> 00:02:22,319
If he didn't tell you about me,
how would you know?

21
00:02:22,403 --> 00:02:26,407
[Haru chuckles] Honestly,
that's not surprising for Legoshi, right?

22
00:02:26,657 --> 00:02:29,118
A normal person
might mention something like that.

23
00:02:29,201 --> 00:02:31,120
Oh, I had a quick question for you.

24
00:02:32,288 --> 00:02:34,623
So, is this Legoshi's mother
in this photo?

25
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:36,876
[Gosha] Yeah.

26
00:02:37,585 --> 00:02:39,378
My daughter takes after her mom.

27
00:02:39,461 --> 00:02:41,005
[Haru] I see that. [chuckles]

28
00:02:41,463 --> 00:02:44,133
I wish I had some juice to offer you.

29
00:02:44,216 --> 00:02:47,094
Legoshi always offers me tea
when I go and visit him.

30
00:02:47,177 --> 00:02:48,387
Oh, is that right?

31
00:02:50,139 --> 00:02:51,181
- [Haru exclaims]
- Oh!

32
00:02:53,017 --> 00:02:54,059
[Haru exclaims]

33
00:02:54,727 --> 00:02:55,811
Huh?

34
00:02:56,645 --> 00:02:58,522
Ah! All disinfected.

35
00:02:58,606 --> 00:03:00,149
What is that spray?

36
00:03:00,232 --> 00:03:03,027
The venom of a Komodo dragon
is very dangerous.

37
00:03:03,110 --> 00:03:06,113
A slightest touch could be deadly
and really ruin your day.

38
00:03:06,572 --> 00:03:07,907
Uh, venom?

39
00:03:08,699 --> 00:03:11,702
Using a stun gun on me
was such a good move.

40
00:03:11,785 --> 00:03:14,705
You don't even have to touch
your opponent to stick it to him.

41
00:03:14,788 --> 00:03:18,125
I apologize again
for zapping you like that.

42
00:03:18,208 --> 00:03:19,710
No, it's on me.

43
00:03:19,793 --> 00:03:21,170
I'm the one who scared you.

44
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:23,505
I got a bit carried away.

45
00:03:24,006 --> 00:03:28,093
I was just happy Legoshi shared info
about someone he really cares about.

46
00:03:28,177 --> 00:03:31,263
I should have told you who I was
and explained what I was doing there.

47
00:03:31,347 --> 00:03:32,348
It's all right.

48
00:03:32,431 --> 00:03:36,310
Legoshi would probably think I'd be
annoyed with him for talking about us.

49
00:03:36,393 --> 00:03:39,730
I guess he just had me so paranoid
about being attacked.

50
00:03:39,813 --> 00:03:43,567
So it sounds like you're pretty
comfortable around my grandson.

51
00:03:43,651 --> 00:03:46,278
- You being a rabbit, he doesn't scare you?
- Huh?

52
00:03:46,362 --> 00:03:48,572
Well, there's always
the risk of devouring,

53
00:03:48,656 --> 00:03:52,368
and his grandpa is a dragon
and he's a wolf on top of that.

54
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:53,869
[chuckles] Oh.

55
00:03:53,953 --> 00:03:55,412
I'm not worried about it.

56
00:03:55,621 --> 00:03:58,040
Sure, there were times when I was scared.

57
00:03:58,123 --> 00:04:02,002
But when a rabbit falls for a wolf,
you've already overcome quite a lot.

58
00:04:02,836 --> 00:04:05,923
Besides, he's not just any wolf.

59
00:04:06,006 --> 00:04:07,466
He's Legoshi, right?

60
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:09,551
Oh, I get that.

61
00:04:09,969 --> 00:04:12,179
Actually reminds me of Toki.

62
00:04:12,263 --> 00:04:14,223
Toki? Was that your wife?

63
00:04:14,306 --> 00:04:15,599
Yeah.

64
00:04:15,683 --> 00:04:18,519
She used to say
the same sort of thing about me.

65
00:04:18,602 --> 00:04:20,187
I won the lottery with her.

66
00:04:20,521 --> 00:04:22,606
I was just a big old Komodo dragon.

67
00:04:22,690 --> 00:04:24,108
[gentle music playing]

68
00:04:25,234 --> 00:04:28,654
<i>When we first met,
we were a couple of teenagers.</i>

69
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:33,158
<i>Everybody had an opinion,
but it was love at first sight.</i>

70
00:04:35,369 --> 00:04:38,163
<i>Now, back in the day,
you stuck to your species.</i>

71
00:04:38,247 --> 00:04:40,040
<i>But we said to hell with that.</i>

72
00:04:41,083 --> 00:04:42,751
<i>The two of us were in love,</i>

73
00:04:42,835 --> 00:04:44,878
<i>and pretty soon, we had a kiddo.</i>

74
00:04:45,379 --> 00:04:47,506
Honey, I think I need a kiss.

75
00:04:47,589 --> 00:04:48,757
I got you, baby.

76
00:04:48,841 --> 00:04:49,842
You're such a cutie.

77
00:04:49,925 --> 00:04:51,427
- Ugh!
- Mmm.

78
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:52,553
Uh...

79
00:04:54,722 --> 00:04:57,141
[Haru] <i>Wait, you did that
with your wife, too?</i>

80
00:04:57,391 --> 00:04:59,977
[Gosha] <i>Yeah,
and she definitely wasn't a fan.</i>

81
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:02,229
<i>She said it wasn't romantic.</i>

82
00:05:04,106 --> 00:05:06,900
<i>I got a kick out of
every day we were together.</i>

83
00:05:07,401 --> 00:05:12,156
<i>I had this beautiful, kind-hearted woman
building a family with a monster like me.</i>

84
00:05:12,781 --> 00:05:13,782
<i>Crazy, right?</i>

85
00:05:13,907 --> 00:05:17,703
{\an8}[Haru] <i>Uh... Well, it doesn't sound like
you were a monster to her.</i>

86
00:05:17,786 --> 00:05:19,330
{\an8}[Gosha] <i>No, that's true.</i>

87
00:05:19,413 --> 00:05:23,042
{\an8}<i>Toki always wished that I would
stop worrying so much</i>

88
00:05:23,125 --> 00:05:25,544
<i>about my venom and the sprays.</i>

89
00:05:26,337 --> 00:05:28,964
<i>It turns out that's what
led to what happened.</i>

90
00:05:29,715 --> 00:05:31,717
<i>She was my whole world.</i>

91
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,594
<i>We only had eyes for each other.</i>

92
00:05:35,971 --> 00:05:37,806
Happy birthday, baby. [chuckles]

93
00:05:38,348 --> 00:05:40,684
[chuckles] Honey, you're so sweet.

94
00:05:41,977 --> 00:05:43,520
You know what I keep thinking about?

95
00:05:43,979 --> 00:05:45,647
There are so many people in this world

96
00:05:45,731 --> 00:05:48,567
and you chose to open up your heart to me.

97
00:05:52,279 --> 00:05:53,405
No! Oh!

98
00:05:53,489 --> 00:05:54,740
Toki, what are you doing?

99
00:05:55,157 --> 00:05:56,241
Where'd I put it?

100
00:05:56,533 --> 00:05:59,244
[grunts] Where is it?
Where's the disinfectant?

101
00:05:59,328 --> 00:06:00,662
It's gotta be here!

102
00:06:00,746 --> 00:06:02,915
Stop. Honey, it's okay.

103
00:06:03,415 --> 00:06:04,666
{\an8}This is what I wanted.

104
00:06:05,501 --> 00:06:08,337
{\an8}So you could love without
worrying about... [whimpers]

105
00:06:08,879 --> 00:06:09,922
{\an8}[Gosha gasps]

106
00:06:12,091 --> 00:06:14,134
{\an8}I hope this helps you let go.

107
00:06:14,218 --> 00:06:16,428
{\an8}You don't need all those fears, my love.

108
00:06:16,512 --> 00:06:18,597
{\an8}[exhales shakily]

109
00:06:19,264 --> 00:06:21,850
[Gosha] <i>It was after that when it hit me.</i>

110
00:06:21,934 --> 00:06:23,018
[Gosha sobbing]

111
00:06:23,102 --> 00:06:25,771
<i>The reason I fell so hard for Toki</i>

112
00:06:26,688 --> 00:06:30,150
was because she was the most
sincere person I ever knew.

113
00:06:30,859 --> 00:06:34,822
If I'd just realized that sooner,
maybe I wouldn't have had to lose her

114
00:06:34,905 --> 00:06:36,448
in the way that I did.

115
00:06:37,074 --> 00:06:39,868
All that to say
I'm happy for you and Legoshi.

116
00:06:40,244 --> 00:06:45,582
My hope for both of you is that you feel
the same kind of happiness that I had.

117
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:49,002
Your whole lives, the two of you together.

118
00:06:49,461 --> 00:06:50,796
We'll be fine.

119
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:53,882
You know, as you were sharing your story,

120
00:06:54,591 --> 00:06:57,469
I thought, I want to know
Legoshi even better.

121
00:06:58,178 --> 00:07:00,055
And I want him to know more of me.

122
00:07:00,722 --> 00:07:03,600
To do that, we have to really be alive.

123
00:07:04,518 --> 00:07:05,686
That's right.

124
00:07:06,812 --> 00:07:10,941
With Toki, it sounds like
you had a very powerful love.

125
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:12,109
{\an8}Yeah.

126
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:17,030
I tell you, I sure miss her.

127
00:07:25,914 --> 00:07:27,583
Why are you crying?

128
00:07:27,666 --> 00:07:29,251
You don't smell that?

129
00:07:29,334 --> 00:07:31,962
My eyes burn. [groaning]

130
00:07:36,133 --> 00:07:37,509
[Legoshi grunts]

131
00:07:37,968 --> 00:07:40,179
[sighs] Fresh air. Thank you.

132
00:07:40,262 --> 00:07:41,930
[child sobbing] I'm sorry, Mama!

133
00:07:42,973 --> 00:07:45,684
[Intel Chief]
I guess he stole something again?

134
00:07:45,767 --> 00:07:47,227
{\an8}Sure, she's a parent.

135
00:07:47,311 --> 00:07:48,645
{\an8}But isn't that a bit much?

136
00:07:48,729 --> 00:07:52,065
{\an8}- Oh, no. He's not really her kid.
- But he called her Mama.

137
00:07:52,149 --> 00:07:54,902
- [Intel Chief] That's his foster mama.
- Don't make me tell you again.

138
00:07:54,985 --> 00:07:56,862
[Legoshi] So he's an orphan then?

139
00:07:56,945 --> 00:07:59,281
[Intel Chief]
That kid was raised by his grandpa.

140
00:07:59,364 --> 00:08:02,493
But it turns out the old man
messed up big time.

141
00:08:03,118 --> 00:08:05,913
Yahya set his sights on him
and he got caught.

142
00:08:05,996 --> 00:08:07,372
You know Yahya, right?

143
00:08:07,456 --> 00:08:08,665
[Legoshi] Yeah.

144
00:08:09,208 --> 00:08:13,337
Once the black devil catches you,
[chuckles] you don't come back.

145
00:08:14,505 --> 00:08:16,340
Fertilizer for carrots.

146
00:08:17,007 --> 00:08:20,052
It's not rare,
kids like him in this Black Market.

147
00:08:20,135 --> 00:08:22,679
- Koho Mama's the one feeding 'em.
- Here's a little something.

148
00:08:22,763 --> 00:08:24,097
[kid gasps, squeals excitedly]

149
00:08:24,181 --> 00:08:25,599
- Mama?
- Ah.

150
00:08:25,891 --> 00:08:31,688
So, Degoshi, do you think it's more
heartless inside or outside of the walls?

151
00:08:33,106 --> 00:08:34,274
[Legoshi] Hmm.

152
00:08:36,568 --> 00:08:38,862
Huh? [gasps]

153
00:08:38,946 --> 00:08:41,990
He carried a week's worth
of food in one go!

154
00:08:42,074 --> 00:08:43,992
- You're amazing, Degoshi!
- Oh, thanks.

155
00:08:44,076 --> 00:08:46,411
I guess manual labor is right up my alley.

156
00:08:46,870 --> 00:08:49,498
- [grunting in distance]
- Huh?

157
00:08:52,584 --> 00:08:54,127
[grunting]

158
00:08:56,171 --> 00:08:59,341
Bean's going to get
as strong as Kyuu for sure.

159
00:08:59,424 --> 00:09:00,717
Kyuu, huh?

160
00:09:00,801 --> 00:09:01,927
It's that rabbit?

161
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:05,764
Yeah! Even though she's a tiny herbivore,
you'd better watch it,

162
00:09:05,847 --> 00:09:09,851
because in the fight club,
she's a top earner. She's a legend.

163
00:09:09,935 --> 00:09:12,437
[Intel Chief]
All the Black Market kids look up to her.

164
00:09:12,521 --> 00:09:14,314
Whoa.

165
00:09:14,398 --> 00:09:17,568
{\an8}- [Intel Chief] A dream.
- A dream?

166
00:09:17,651 --> 00:09:20,279
She gives the kids a reason to dream.

167
00:09:20,362 --> 00:09:22,698
Like, she's a shining star.

168
00:09:22,781 --> 00:09:23,907
Just look at her.

169
00:09:23,991 --> 00:09:25,701
They want to be like that.

170
00:09:25,784 --> 00:09:27,578
When they've got someone like her,

171
00:09:27,661 --> 00:09:30,414
these kids get inspired
and hold their heads up.

172
00:09:30,497 --> 00:09:32,499
It's about more than just a fight club.

173
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:36,503
Having someone to look up to
can be really powerful.

174
00:09:36,962 --> 00:09:39,881
Look down and you just
trip over one another.

175
00:09:39,965 --> 00:09:42,551
Look sideways
and you're really just glaring.

176
00:09:43,176 --> 00:09:46,054
I mean, if we can be inspired,
at least for a little bit,

177
00:09:46,138 --> 00:09:48,348
maybe fighting's not the only option.

178
00:09:48,432 --> 00:09:50,267
Same thing for high society.

179
00:09:51,643 --> 00:09:55,564
[Legoshi] <i>I wonder if we could all
share the same dream.</i>

180
00:09:56,607 --> 00:09:58,900
<i>Could the Black Market
and regular society?</i>

181
00:09:58,984 --> 00:10:00,777
<i>Could carnivores and herbivores?</i>

182
00:10:02,029 --> 00:10:03,780
<i>Could they live in peace?</i>

183
00:10:11,538 --> 00:10:12,748
[Louis] <i>What do I do?</i>

184
00:10:13,332 --> 00:10:14,750
<i>I could disappear.</i>

185
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:16,460
<i>No, that won't work.</i>

186
00:10:16,543 --> 00:10:18,253
<i>What does running away solve?</i>

187
00:10:19,046 --> 00:10:21,465
- [Azuki] Louis?
- [Louis] <i>Face this thing already.</i>

188
00:10:21,548 --> 00:10:22,591
<i>Come on.</i>

189
00:10:22,674 --> 00:10:24,593
I just had a wonderful bath.

190
00:10:24,968 --> 00:10:27,304
[Louis] Oh. Well, that sure was fast.

191
00:10:27,804 --> 00:10:29,765
<i>You coward. Say it.</i>

192
00:10:29,848 --> 00:10:31,308
<i>Tell her you can't do this.</i>

193
00:10:31,391 --> 00:10:33,560
<i>Not with an herbivore. She needs to know.</i>

194
00:10:33,644 --> 00:10:35,228
[Azuki] I'm glad you came over.

195
00:10:35,312 --> 00:10:38,315
I was worried you might turn me down
when I invited you.

196
00:10:38,398 --> 00:10:40,942
[Louis] <i>It's not like I didn't know
we'd be alone together.</i>

197
00:10:41,026 --> 00:10:42,653
<i>So why'd I even come?</i>

198
00:10:42,736 --> 00:10:44,571
<i>All I have to do is say something.</i>

199
00:10:46,281 --> 00:10:48,367
<i>No. Breaking off the engagement...</i>

200
00:10:49,034 --> 00:10:50,619
<i>That's impossible. I can't.</i>

201
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:54,498
<i>At the same time, I'm just... I'm stuck.</i>

202
00:10:54,581 --> 00:10:56,750
- So, should I order some room service?
- Uh...

203
00:10:57,417 --> 00:10:59,294
You haven't had dinner yet, right?

204
00:10:59,378 --> 00:11:00,879
The room service here is so--

205
00:11:00,962 --> 00:11:02,464
[grunts]

206
00:11:02,547 --> 00:11:03,507
Huh?

207
00:11:03,590 --> 00:11:06,301
You're doing a lot of worrying
and a lot of talking.

208
00:11:06,385 --> 00:11:08,011
Why don't you just try and relax?

209
00:11:08,095 --> 00:11:09,805
[grunts] No, just hang on.

210
00:11:09,888 --> 00:11:10,931
[Azuki gasps]

211
00:11:11,014 --> 00:11:12,224
[Louis gasps]

212
00:11:14,935 --> 00:11:18,397
- No, uh, it's just--
- You're not the only one.

213
00:11:18,897 --> 00:11:21,483
{\an8}You think it's just you
trying to make this work? You're wrong.

214
00:11:21,566 --> 00:11:22,651
But it's not you.

215
00:11:22,734 --> 00:11:24,069
Forgive me.

216
00:11:24,152 --> 00:11:26,738
I know we both feel pressure
to please our families.

217
00:11:26,822 --> 00:11:29,116
Is it that you're just
not attracted to me?

218
00:11:29,199 --> 00:11:30,283
No, that's not it at all.

219
00:11:30,367 --> 00:11:32,911
Then show me.
Kiss me, take me in your arms.

220
00:11:32,994 --> 00:11:34,663
- Is that so wrong?
- [sighs]

221
00:11:35,539 --> 00:11:36,748
I wish I could.

222
00:11:37,541 --> 00:11:38,417
[breath shudders]

223
00:11:39,126 --> 00:11:40,836
{\an8}It's nothing to do with you.

224
00:11:41,461 --> 00:11:43,630
{\an8}It's just stuff I've got to work out.

225
00:11:43,713 --> 00:11:44,965
{\an8}For me.

226
00:11:45,048 --> 00:11:46,883
{\an8}It's a thing with herbivores.

227
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:47,968
{\an8}[Azuki] Uh...

228
00:11:48,051 --> 00:11:49,428
{\an8}I have feelings.

229
00:11:50,011 --> 00:11:51,138
{\an8}What I mean...

230
00:11:51,221 --> 00:11:55,267
{\an8}I think I'm only attracted to carnivores,
but that's not the only part.

231
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:59,187
It's just... It's hard
to explain to my father.

232
00:11:59,271 --> 00:12:03,567
It seems like he just sees me
as the heir to his Horns Conglomerate.

233
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:05,819
Profit matters more to him than me.

234
00:12:06,570 --> 00:12:08,697
{\an8}I'm sorry. I know it's a lot.

235
00:12:09,573 --> 00:12:12,451
{\an8}I don't pretend to understand
the carnivore thing.

236
00:12:12,534 --> 00:12:14,286
{\an8}I just feel safe around them.

237
00:12:15,287 --> 00:12:16,746
I don't understand it.

238
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:20,750
But when I'm with carnivores,
even their scent puts me at ease.

239
00:12:22,294 --> 00:12:24,921
You can call off the engagement
if you want.

240
00:12:25,005 --> 00:12:28,675
After all, I might never
be able to make love to you.

241
00:12:29,301 --> 00:12:33,555
The point of our marriage is to produce
an heir, and that may never happen.

242
00:12:33,638 --> 00:12:35,557
I'm sorry, Azuki. Uh...

243
00:12:37,434 --> 00:12:38,810
I understand.

244
00:12:38,894 --> 00:12:41,938
And if that's how it is, okay.
It's all right.

245
00:12:42,022 --> 00:12:43,523
You can let go of any pressure

246
00:12:43,607 --> 00:12:44,900
- to make love to me.
- Huh?

247
00:12:44,983 --> 00:12:48,236
Listen, Louis,
we can still focus on our goal.

248
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,572
You and I are meant
to unite our two families.

249
00:12:51,031 --> 00:12:54,534
We will still need a child, but
there are other ways to make that happen.

250
00:12:54,618 --> 00:12:55,911
[Louis stammers]

251
00:12:55,994 --> 00:12:57,621
And don't get me wrong.

252
00:12:57,704 --> 00:13:00,874
I was certainly looking forward
to something romantic with you.

253
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:04,669
But here we are.
We'll just have to adapt and roll with it.

254
00:13:04,961 --> 00:13:07,255
That's the key to a successful business.

255
00:13:07,714 --> 00:13:09,132
What are you saying?

256
00:13:09,716 --> 00:13:11,510
We're just shifting our priorities.

257
00:13:11,593 --> 00:13:14,513
You and I will just take romance
off the table as an option,

258
00:13:14,596 --> 00:13:16,473
we can be together without having sex.

259
00:13:16,556 --> 00:13:17,766
Seriously?

260
00:13:17,849 --> 00:13:20,268
You're telling me, after all this,

261
00:13:20,352 --> 00:13:22,437
that we should still go through
with the marriage?

262
00:13:22,521 --> 00:13:23,980
Yes, just like we planned.

263
00:13:24,064 --> 00:13:25,815
- That's crazy.
- And why is that?

264
00:13:25,899 --> 00:13:28,318
{\an8}I don't want you to be
in an unhappy marriage.

265
00:13:29,027 --> 00:13:31,613
{\an8}- And besides that--
- Louis...

266
00:13:32,489 --> 00:13:35,450
- I think you have the wrong idea about me.
- [exhales]

267
00:13:35,534 --> 00:13:36,868
Let me explain.

268
00:13:36,952 --> 00:13:39,371
For me, marriage itself is the goal.

269
00:13:39,454 --> 00:13:40,664
Huh?

270
00:13:41,248 --> 00:13:42,457
{\an8}You don't have to worry.

271
00:13:42,541 --> 00:13:43,959
{\an8}This isn't a problem.

272
00:13:45,043 --> 00:13:50,131
We can still be partners, even if it
turns out that we don't end up as lovers.

273
00:13:50,215 --> 00:13:51,800
- Business partners.
- [sighs]

274
00:13:52,634 --> 00:13:55,136
Are you sure that arrangement
works for you?

275
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,388
Yes.

276
00:13:56,471 --> 00:14:01,476
My main concern is growing the company
that down the line will be my inheritance.

277
00:14:02,143 --> 00:14:03,603
And through our marriage,

278
00:14:03,687 --> 00:14:06,648
my Ogura Foods business gains a legacy.

279
00:14:06,731 --> 00:14:08,942
And with your Horns Conglomerate,

280
00:14:09,025 --> 00:14:10,860
you'll be able to secure its future.

281
00:14:11,194 --> 00:14:12,237
Uh...

282
00:14:13,864 --> 00:14:15,031
[Louis chuckles softly]

283
00:14:17,993 --> 00:14:20,161
LION

284
00:14:21,621 --> 00:14:23,874
So you're really doing this, huh?

285
00:14:23,957 --> 00:14:24,958
Of course.

286
00:14:25,041 --> 00:14:26,543
You guys know the deal.

287
00:14:26,626 --> 00:14:29,838
You want to do this Meat Appreciation Day
turf war, you need a boss.

288
00:14:29,921 --> 00:14:33,216
Just so you know, this doesn't mean
I accept you as our boss.

289
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:36,636
I know, I know. It's just for now.

290
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:39,222
Otherwise,
we'll have to wait another year.

291
00:14:39,306 --> 00:14:42,434
The Inari-Gumi, Doku-Gumi,
and Madara-Gumi are all entered.

292
00:14:42,517 --> 00:14:46,438
If they take our turf from us, they'll
just laugh at us every time we see 'em.

293
00:14:47,314 --> 00:14:49,566
Representative.

294
00:14:49,649 --> 00:14:53,028
Ah! A-ga-ta. There.

295
00:14:54,237 --> 00:14:56,197
Hmm. Perfect!

296
00:14:56,281 --> 00:14:57,449
LEADER
AGATA

297
00:14:57,532 --> 00:15:00,493
[exhales] All right. I'll go enter us.

298
00:15:00,577 --> 00:15:01,912
Uh, hold on, hold on.

299
00:15:01,995 --> 00:15:04,831
Wouldn't it be better if we all
go together to show our strength?

300
00:15:04,915 --> 00:15:07,918
It ain't forever,
but a representative's a representative.

301
00:15:08,001 --> 00:15:09,127
You got that right.

302
00:15:11,296 --> 00:15:14,591
[tune whistling in distance]

303
00:15:15,216 --> 00:15:16,551
[breathes shakily]

304
00:15:19,429 --> 00:15:20,722
[footsteps approaching]

305
00:15:20,805 --> 00:15:22,182
That the boss?

306
00:15:27,062 --> 00:15:28,980
Ah, you're all here.

307
00:15:29,064 --> 00:15:31,358
Well, this is quite the homecoming.

308
00:15:31,441 --> 00:15:32,734
[gasps]

309
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:35,028
Huh?

310
00:15:38,198 --> 00:15:40,784
[Melon breathes deeply]

311
00:15:40,867 --> 00:15:42,243
What am I looking at?

312
00:15:42,327 --> 00:15:43,411
SHISHI-GUMI

313
00:15:43,495 --> 00:15:46,498
[Agata] Well, we were planning
to enter the turf war.

314
00:15:46,581 --> 00:15:47,958
[Melon] Huh.

315
00:15:48,541 --> 00:15:50,418
Meat Appreciation Day.

316
00:15:50,502 --> 00:15:52,295
What perfect timing.

317
00:15:52,754 --> 00:15:55,090
I had my eye on a certain little rabbit,

318
00:15:55,173 --> 00:15:59,511
but, alas, I wonder
when I'll tie up that loose end.

319
00:15:59,928 --> 00:16:02,555
Well, it's the day to love meat, right?

320
00:16:02,639 --> 00:16:05,183
To eat her on that day... Oh.

321
00:16:06,267 --> 00:16:07,394
Huh?

322
00:16:07,477 --> 00:16:08,687
[shudders]

323
00:16:09,688 --> 00:16:12,649
"Representative Agata."

324
00:16:13,191 --> 00:16:15,860
[Melon laughs condescendingly]

325
00:16:16,444 --> 00:16:19,698
I'm standing in the presence
of a big shot, huh?

326
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:25,412
I have to ask,
am I really this easy for you to replace?

327
00:16:25,495 --> 00:16:28,331
{\an8}Uh, well, what can we do, boss?

328
00:16:28,415 --> 00:16:32,794
{\an8}We couldn't find you,
and so, uh, I ended up filling in.

329
00:16:32,877 --> 00:16:34,587
[Melon sighs]

330
00:16:34,671 --> 00:16:38,675
[laughs maniacally]

331
00:16:38,758 --> 00:16:42,512
So you, uh, thought you would
just step right in?

332
00:16:42,595 --> 00:16:44,097
- [grunts]
- [groans]

333
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,724
[Melon snarls, sighs]

334
00:16:46,391 --> 00:16:49,060
I was kind enough to give you that scar.

335
00:16:49,144 --> 00:16:52,188
Yet I'm sensing you still don't get it.

336
00:16:52,272 --> 00:16:53,606
[gasps]

337
00:16:54,315 --> 00:16:55,525
[grunts]

338
00:16:55,942 --> 00:16:59,362
{\an8}You might be able to write
your name down as the boss,

339
00:16:59,446 --> 00:17:01,823
{\an8}but good luck getting any further.

340
00:17:01,906 --> 00:17:06,870
{\an8}In fact, I dare you to find someone
who could lead this pathetic crew.

341
00:17:09,372 --> 00:17:11,750
[Melon] <i>You won't find someone like me.</i>

342
00:17:12,625 --> 00:17:15,295
<i>My mom had a hard time grasping that fact.</i>

343
00:17:15,378 --> 00:17:19,257
[hissing]

344
00:17:19,340 --> 00:17:20,550
<i>Poor Mom.</i>

345
00:17:20,633 --> 00:17:22,594
<i>She said she loved me,</i>

346
00:17:23,678 --> 00:17:27,682
<i>but she was always hoping
to see a bit more Dad in me.</i>

347
00:17:27,766 --> 00:17:29,434
[horror sting]

348
00:17:30,310 --> 00:17:31,895
<i>Never happened, though.</i>

349
00:17:32,479 --> 00:17:34,147
<i>Be a weak herbivore?</i>

350
00:17:34,230 --> 00:17:35,899
[chuckles] <i>No, thanks.</i>

351
00:17:35,982 --> 00:17:39,736
<i>I needed her to understand that...</i>

352
00:17:40,153 --> 00:17:41,362
- [thuds]
- [splatters]

353
00:17:41,905 --> 00:17:43,490
<i>...I'm not like her.</i>

354
00:17:43,573 --> 00:17:45,450
<i>I'm not like Dad.</i>

355
00:17:45,533 --> 00:17:47,368
<i>I am not like anyone.</i>

356
00:17:48,119 --> 00:17:49,454
<i>I'm one of one.</i>

357
00:17:49,996 --> 00:17:52,665
<i>No one can take my place.</i>

358
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:57,045
- [gunshot]
- [Agata screaming]

359
00:17:57,128 --> 00:17:59,631
- [groaning]
- [Melon laughs]

360
00:18:00,090 --> 00:18:02,217
Now, talk about taking places,

361
00:18:02,717 --> 00:18:05,887
can someone else
take the pain in your place?

362
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:08,348
That pain is yours alone.

363
00:18:10,183 --> 00:18:12,435
Because you're on your own.

364
00:18:12,977 --> 00:18:16,064
If you think you can do it,
step right up then.

365
00:18:16,147 --> 00:18:18,566
Take the boss' seat with your own hands.

366
00:18:19,192 --> 00:18:21,986
You want to get rid of something,
you crush it.

367
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:24,781
Have the courage to forge your own path.

368
00:18:24,864 --> 00:18:28,034
That's how we do things
around here, right? Ha!

369
00:18:28,493 --> 00:18:31,621
After all, you guys said it yourselves

370
00:18:32,330 --> 00:18:35,208
when you talked about
being worthy of your manes,

371
00:18:35,291 --> 00:18:38,044
or whatever that proverb was, [chuckles]

372
00:18:38,711 --> 00:18:40,713
what's the criteria for that?

373
00:18:40,797 --> 00:18:43,007
What makes you worthy of your manes?

374
00:18:43,091 --> 00:18:45,760
Um... Demonstrating strength.

375
00:18:46,594 --> 00:18:47,846
[Agata groaning]

376
00:18:47,929 --> 00:18:49,639
[Melon laughs] Oh.

377
00:18:49,722 --> 00:18:50,932
Is that right?

378
00:18:51,766 --> 00:18:55,103
Strength comes from truly being free.

379
00:18:55,186 --> 00:18:57,522
The weak love their shackles.

380
00:18:57,605 --> 00:19:00,567
Do what you want to do.
Eat what you want to eat.

381
00:19:01,151 --> 00:19:02,235
Really...

382
00:19:02,944 --> 00:19:05,697
tell me what's so wrong with living free?

383
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:08,616
Isn't that what
the Black Market's all about?

384
00:19:10,326 --> 00:19:13,204
[Agata] <i>This devil fits right in
at the Black Market.</i>

385
00:19:14,914 --> 00:19:17,750
[gasps] <i>It all makes sense.</i>

386
00:19:18,668 --> 00:19:21,171
<i>He's a carnivore and an herbivore.</i>

387
00:19:22,088 --> 00:19:23,756
<i>He's the real deal.</i>

388
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:26,009
<i>The king of beasts.</i>

389
00:19:26,926 --> 00:19:29,345
[Agata groaning]

390
00:19:33,141 --> 00:19:34,309
[Melon] Huh?

391
00:19:35,977 --> 00:19:38,771
I'll follow you till the end, boss,
I swear to you.

392
00:19:39,230 --> 00:19:40,899
- [groans]
- Agata...

393
00:19:41,774 --> 00:19:44,569
I think we all know
you're insane and broken.

394
00:19:44,652 --> 00:19:47,822
Still, our pride's the only one
that has your back.

395
00:19:47,906 --> 00:19:49,407
You're on our team.

396
00:19:49,741 --> 00:19:52,368
You can take my arm, my mane.

397
00:19:52,452 --> 00:19:54,120
With you leading the Shishi-Gumi,

398
00:19:54,204 --> 00:19:58,124
we're all stronger,
and no one will dare stand in our way.

399
00:19:58,625 --> 00:20:00,084
[stammers]

400
00:20:00,793 --> 00:20:02,253
Yeah, that's right.

401
00:20:02,337 --> 00:20:04,339
There's no one as crazy as you.

402
00:20:04,756 --> 00:20:06,216
Aren't you smart?

403
00:20:06,299 --> 00:20:08,593
Otherwise, I wouldn't be this fun.

404
00:20:08,676 --> 00:20:12,513
All right, guys.
Here's the next adventure.

405
00:20:15,558 --> 00:20:16,893
Melda?

406
00:20:16,976 --> 00:20:20,146
You haven't messed
with that stuff yet, huh?

407
00:20:20,230 --> 00:20:22,732
Everyone who thinks
they've got it all figured out,

408
00:20:22,815 --> 00:20:26,444
they're about to truly live
their lives for the first time.

409
00:20:26,527 --> 00:20:28,905
Let's get even darker.

410
00:20:29,489 --> 00:20:34,118
Time for us to become the pitch-black
beast kings of the Black Market.

411
00:20:34,202 --> 00:20:35,536
Shishi-Gumi!

412
00:20:36,663 --> 00:20:37,956
- Yeah!
- All right.

413
00:20:38,039 --> 00:20:39,082
All right.

414
00:20:39,165 --> 00:20:40,375
- Yeah.
- All right.

415
00:20:45,004 --> 00:20:47,006
[intense drum music playing]

416
00:20:51,511 --> 00:20:53,429
SAFETY FIRST

417
00:20:53,513 --> 00:20:55,598
[lively chatter]

418
00:20:55,682 --> 00:21:00,770
It's that time of the year when
the Black Market territories are decided.

419
00:21:00,853 --> 00:21:04,774
This year's participants
for Meat Appreciation Day are

420
00:21:04,857 --> 00:21:07,110
- the Inari-Gumi--
- [crowd cheering]

421
00:21:07,193 --> 00:21:09,570
- the Madara-Gumi--
- [crowd cheering]

422
00:21:09,654 --> 00:21:11,656
- the Doku-Gumi!
- [crowd cheering]

423
00:21:11,739 --> 00:21:13,283
Where's the Shishi-Gumi?

424
00:21:13,366 --> 00:21:14,701
Go! Move it!

425
00:21:14,784 --> 00:21:16,119
What are you looking at?

426
00:21:16,202 --> 00:21:18,288
- What the hell?
- [lion] Make way! Coming through!

427
00:21:18,371 --> 00:21:19,914
- Move it, pal!
- Watch yourself.

428
00:21:19,998 --> 00:21:21,708
Give us some room, huh?

429
00:21:22,292 --> 00:21:24,294
[intense drum music continuing]

430
00:21:32,927 --> 00:21:34,762
MELON

431
00:21:34,846 --> 00:21:37,724
{\an8}- Is that the boss of the Shishi-Gumi?
- Yeah! Let's go!

432
00:21:37,807 --> 00:21:40,184
- Is that a mix?
- I've never seen him before.

433
00:21:40,268 --> 00:21:41,269
Is that...

434
00:21:41,352 --> 00:21:42,478
[both panting]

435
00:21:47,233 --> 00:21:50,445
[Legoshi]
Have you ever seen this guy around here?

436
00:21:51,404 --> 00:21:52,822
A gazelle?

437
00:21:52,905 --> 00:21:55,658
- No, he's a mix.
- Hey! Hey, Degoshi!

438
00:21:55,742 --> 00:21:56,993
We found Melon.

439
00:21:57,535 --> 00:21:58,536
Huh?

440
00:21:58,619 --> 00:21:59,871
{\an8}Well, where is he?

441
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,999
[closing theme song playing]
